Z||000000||Wade87GT||10-02-2000||11:27 AM||||I was at the Pontiac dealer Saturday and the new Aztec is putting out 185 HP from a pushrod 3.4, and it's also a transverse set-up. Has anybody looked into this further as our next "simple" engine swap?||||reg||5
Z||000001||HugGRRRFiero||10-02-2000||11:55 AM||||Sorry, I don't know if anyone has done a V8 conversion on an Aztek yet?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>I believe you can find the same exact 3.4 in a Montana Van.  Personally, I'd use the Aztek over the Montana for the donor.  That way you could always weld up a trailer tongue on the Aztek and use it as a small camper trailer if you wanted.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Hey they say it's the most versatile vehicle on the planet.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">||||reg||3
